\end_inset

 where their purpose it clearly visible.
 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathcal{G}_{x}$
\end_inset

 highlights the horizontal edges in 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathbf{I}$
\end_inset

and 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathcal{G}_{y}$
\end_inset

 the vertical.
 We combine the two mappings into the Sobel filter
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
\mathcal{G}=\begin{bmatrix}\sqrt{\left[\mathcal{G}_{y}\right]^{2}_{1\,1}+\left[\mathcal{G}_{y}\right]^{2}_{1\,1}} & \sqrt{\left[\mathcal{G}_{y}\right]^{2}_{1\,2}+\left[\mathcal{G}_{y}\right]^{2}_{1\,2}} & \cdots & \sqrt{\left[\mathcal{G}_{y}\right]^{2}_{1\,642}+\left[\mathcal{G}_{y}\right]^{2}_{1\,642}}\\
\sqrt{\left[\mathcal{G}_{y}\right]^{2}_{2\,1}+\left[\mathcal{G}_{y}\right]^{2}_{2\,1}} & \sqrt{\left[\mathcal{G}_{y}\right]^{2}_{2\,2}+\left[\mathcal{G}_{y}\right]^{2}_{2\,2}} & \cdots & \sqrt{\left[\mathcal{G}_{y}\right]^{2}_{2\,642}+\left[\mathcal{G}_{y}\right]^{2}_{2\,642}}\\
\vdots & \vdots & \ddots & \vdots\\
